WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.319
The purpose of my program is to draw a triangle, a

2
00:00:03.319 --> 00:00:06.240
square, and a pentagon, each in a new color.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.153
My code works by using variables and events in this

4
00:00:09.153 --> 00:00:11.857
block code. The variables keep track of the shape it's

5
00:00:11.857 --> 00:00:13.960
drawing, and the event starts the program.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.591
When the green flag is clicked, the reset block clears

7
00:00:17.591 --> 00:00:20.700
the stage and puts the sprite at its starting spot.

8
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.670
Then the pen down block gets it ready to draw.

9
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.045
Next, the set block makes num sides three, so the

10
00:00:27.045 --> 00:00:28.830
program will draw a triangle.

11
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.893
Then the second set block makes side length eighty, so

12
00:00:32.893 --> 00:00:35.170
it moves eighty steps for every side.

13
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.180
The repeat uses num sides, so it runs three times.

14
00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.457
Each time, it moves side length steps and turns three

15
00:00:42.457 --> 00:00:45.438
hundred sixty degrees divided by num sides. The result

16
00:00:45.438 --> 00:00:48.310
of this is one hundred twenty degrees for each turn.

17
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.690
Then it waits one second.

18
00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.440
Then the pen up block lifts the pen, so it can move

19
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.510
without drawing,

20
00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.808
and it moves side length plus thirty, which is a hundred

21
00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:01.270
ten steps, to get to the next spot.

22
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.567
The change pen hue block gives the next shape a new

23
00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:07.360
color, and pen down gets it ready to draw again.

24
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.197
The change block adds one to num sides, so now it's

25
00:01:11.197 --> 00:01:11.540
four.

26
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.272
So the same repeat now runs four times, and each turn is

27
00:01:15.272 --> 00:01:17.500
ninety degrees, which draws a square.

28
00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.286
The number of sides went up. But side length is still

29
00:01:21.286 --> 00:01:24.290
eighty, so every side is just as long as before.

30
00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:28.077
Then it lifts the pen and moves side length plus fifty,

31
00:01:28.077 --> 00:01:30.710
so there's more room for the bigger shape.

32
00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.670
It changes the color again,

33
00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.390
and changes num sides by one, so now it's five.

34
00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.370
That makes the last repeat run five times,

35
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.790
and each turn is seventy two degrees, which draws a

36
00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.330
pentagon.

37
00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.595
It keeps drawing sides until all five are done, and it

38
00:01:48.595 --> 00:01:50.530
ends right back up at the start.

39
00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.587
Variables in programming are different than math. In

40
00:01:57.587 --> 00:02:00.616
math, a variable is one number that doesn't change. In

41
00:02:00.616 --> 00:02:03.758
code, a variable stores something, and it can change. In

42
00:02:03.758 --> 00:02:06.731
my program, num sides starts at three. Then while the

43
00:02:06.731 --> 00:02:09.648
program runs, it changes to four. Then it changes to

44
00:02:09.648 --> 00:02:12.677
five. That's how the same repeat draws three different

45
00:02:12.677 --> 00:02:13.070
shapes.

